WEBVTT

01:41.851 --> 01:45.605
<i>I know you'll be able to, with your eyes.</i>

01:51.945 --> 01:54.197
<i>With your vision, I'm sure you can see it.</i>

01:55.949 --> 01:57.784
<i>How's this, Dad?</i>

01:59.077 --> 02:01.454
<i>I'm sure that Yujiro Hanma
wanted to see this.</i>

02:02.872 --> 02:05.959
<i>I've brought it from far, far away.</i>

02:07.210 --> 02:10.672
<i>T. Rex's rival, the Triceratops.</i>

02:13.216 --> 02:15.844
<i>The dynamism of the young man's movements,</i>

02:17.971 --> 02:20.348
<i>the heaviness of his feet
as he planted them,</i>

02:21.307 --> 02:24.352
<i>the look that conveys
the ancient fighting spirit</i>

02:25.478 --> 02:28.606
<i>made everyone there think the same thing.</i>

02:29.357 --> 02:31.609
<i>The will behind this form,</i>

02:32.527 --> 02:34.612
<i>the weight this form is endowed with,</i>

02:35.530 --> 02:37.949
<i>and the murderous intent this form invokes</i>

02:38.449 --> 02:41.327
<i>were made thoroughly clear
to everyone there.</i>

02:41.911 --> 02:43.830
I... I can see it.

02:43.913 --> 02:45.206
Awesome.

02:45.290 --> 02:46.374
It's huge.

02:46.457 --> 02:49.377
It's giant. Six meters tall. No, eight.

02:50.795 --> 02:55.633
<i>And especially through his father's eyes
with their godly perception.</i>

02:57.051 --> 02:57.927
<i>By now,</i>

02:58.720 --> 03:01.389
<i>the young man's body had dissipated...</i>

03:04.184 --> 03:08.146
<i>and only his will that created
the illusion had taken physical form.</i>

03:09.647 --> 03:13.026
<i>From the time of his youth,
he'd often thought about them.</i>

03:13.776 --> 03:17.780
<i>As he awakened to his body's will,
he'd often thought about them.</i>

03:18.406 --> 03:22.535
<i>He still thought about them
after becoming an adult, to be honest.</i>

03:23.411 --> 03:25.288
<i>Not just five or six times.</i>

03:25.872 --> 03:29.042
<i>Just how darn strong were these guys?</i>

03:31.419 --> 03:32.420
<i>Come at me.</i>

03:33.254 --> 03:34.923
<i>I'll savor this, so come at me.</i>

03:35.590 --> 03:38.927
<i>Just like I've dreamed, come at me!</i>

03:42.931 --> 03:45.683
<i>He let loose! At last,
he used what he'd never used before,</i>

03:45.767 --> 03:47.227
<i>the Triceratops Fist!</i>

04:07.830 --> 04:09.207
Jesus!

04:11.292 --> 04:12.168
That car!

04:19.050 --> 04:20.677
They flipped it over!

04:25.098 --> 04:26.266
I'll admit,

04:26.975 --> 04:31.646
the strength it takes to steamroll through
my body, which far surpasses 100 kilos,

04:32.230 --> 04:35.566
while tearing up the asphalt,
and even flip a car,

04:36.484 --> 04:39.487
isn't that of your body,
which barely weighs 70 kilos.

04:42.448 --> 04:45.076
<i>I fully enjoyed
that primitive physical strength.</i>

04:56.796 --> 04:58.006
Now then,

04:58.673 --> 05:01.050
the ideal of <i>Shokeiken,</i>

05:01.134 --> 05:05.263
that is to say, the style
that should be strived for...

05:07.348 --> 05:09.267
I'll tell you what it is.

05:10.351 --> 05:13.896
Yushoken, <i>which imitates
the bear's fighting style.</i>

05:15.189 --> 05:18.151
Kokeiken, <i>derived from the tiger's force.</i>

05:19.235 --> 05:23.156
Toroken, <i>which incorporates
the fighting style of the mantis.</i>

05:24.073 --> 05:26.659
And then there is your original,

05:27.452 --> 05:30.163
Kyoryuken, <i>the dinosaur fist.</i>

05:30.747 --> 05:33.166
One may vary the forms,

05:34.208 --> 05:36.502
but in essence, they're just imitations.

05:37.503 --> 05:38.546
Interesting.

05:39.839 --> 05:41.424
So, what are you gonna show me?

05:42.050 --> 05:43.134
Don't miss it,

05:44.010 --> 05:46.512
the ideal form of <i>Shokeiken.</i>

05:52.643 --> 05:56.439
<i>His father ridiculed it, saying
it was essentially just an imitation.</i>

06:07.867 --> 06:11.454
<i>What's he going to incorporate?
What's he going to mimic?</i>

06:12.038 --> 06:13.456
You moron.

06:13.539 --> 06:17.460
I'm totally making up
this movement, of course.

06:18.044 --> 06:18.920
What?!

06:34.143 --> 06:34.977
<i>What was that?</i>

06:38.689 --> 06:39.524
Huh?

06:46.614 --> 06:47.907
I get it now.

06:48.991 --> 06:50.868
That's so totally like you, Dad.

06:50.952 --> 06:52.787
Hey, isn't that...

06:54.247 --> 06:58.126
<i>Shokeiken</i> is derived from
the fighting style of a stronger fighter.

06:58.960 --> 07:03.131
That's why it culminates
in the Yujiro Hanma form!

07:05.007 --> 07:07.135
That's the shape of the light we just saw!

07:08.219 --> 07:09.429
Sorry, man.

07:10.096 --> 07:12.723
I don't know
of anything stronger than this.

07:14.517 --> 07:16.144
<i>There's no doubt about that.</i>

07:17.186 --> 07:18.646
<i>My dad lifted his arms aloft,</i>

07:19.564 --> 07:21.858
<i>then let loose a blast into the empty air.</i>

07:23.151 --> 07:27.405
<i>The invisible force flew through the air
and slammed into me.</i>

07:29.782 --> 07:32.410
<i>That's what it seemed to feel like.</i>

07:34.245 --> 07:36.664
<i>His round kick drew
a beautiful arc through the air.</i>

07:37.832 --> 07:41.169
<i>Then, just like with the punch,
an invisible force was unleashed.</i>

07:42.378 --> 07:45.173
<i>That force had already gained
a physical form</i>

07:45.756 --> 07:48.759
<i>and could be clearly seen.</i>

07:55.099 --> 07:57.185
<i>My dad's words were no lie.</i>

07:58.936 --> 08:02.815
<i>Yujiro Hanma himself
was performing</i> "Yujiroken."

08:07.653 --> 08:11.908
<i>It was powerful, natural, and beautiful.</i>

08:13.618 --> 08:15.411
<i>The real thing imitated himself.</i>

08:16.829 --> 08:20.333
<i>No other form of</i> Shokeiken
<i>could be more natural.</i>

08:21.250 --> 08:24.337
How was my own form?

08:25.588 --> 08:26.839
Dad.

08:27.673 --> 08:30.343
You have a fist as hard as Yujiro Hanma.

08:31.344 --> 08:33.846
You have muscles as powerful as Yujiro.

08:34.764 --> 08:36.682
You have the speed of Yujiro.

08:38.100 --> 08:43.356
Yujiro Hanma performing Yujiro Hanma
is obviously going to be perfect.

08:46.192 --> 08:47.360
But, Dad.

08:47.985 --> 08:48.861
Yes?

08:49.570 --> 08:54.116
The virtue of a fighting form
is never in its appearance.

08:57.954 --> 09:01.207
Really? It's not about appearances?

09:01.290 --> 09:02.875
What is it about, then?

09:03.459 --> 09:06.629
Well, if you don't know,
I'll have to teach you.

09:08.548 --> 09:09.715
<i>That's right.</i>

09:09.799 --> 09:13.135
<i>The ideal form is always useful in battle.</i>

09:15.513 --> 09:18.641
<i>I've got to teach my father that.</i>

09:26.274 --> 09:27.400
Shit.

09:28.067 --> 09:30.987
I can't remember the last time
I went down like this.

09:31.487 --> 09:33.573
What? He went down?

09:34.073 --> 09:37.410
What? What on earth just happened?

09:39.495 --> 09:41.330
Now, his father just...

09:41.414 --> 09:42.540
Did he trip?

09:42.623 --> 09:44.875
It looked like he stumbled.

09:46.210 --> 09:51.424
<i>That brat. You've already reached
that level at the tender age of 18, huh?</i>

09:52.258 --> 09:57.930
I had already conceded that my son,
Baki, was the finest of toys.

09:59.890 --> 10:01.684
However,

10:02.226 --> 10:05.688
I never knew that you had
that kind of thing up your sleeve.

10:07.315 --> 10:09.775
<i>I involuntarily transmitted a signal.</i>

10:09.859 --> 10:13.904
<i>You used the half-second it takes
for the brain to command the body</i>

10:13.988 --> 10:15.531
<i>to move to your advantage.</i>

10:16.991 --> 10:17.908
Well done.

10:19.410 --> 10:21.704
I'll pat your head. Come here.

10:23.914 --> 10:27.418
What are you saying? That's ludicrous!

10:27.501 --> 10:30.212
<i>What the heck is this?!</i>

10:30.296 --> 10:32.673
Don't be shy. Come here.

10:32.757 --> 10:33.799
This is a fight!

10:34.383 --> 10:37.720
It's only natural for me
to praise my son's great achievement.

10:42.141 --> 10:42.975
<i>What?</i>

10:45.144 --> 10:45.978
<i>Tears...</i>

10:47.313 --> 10:48.356
<i>What the...</i>

10:49.231 --> 10:51.067
<i>What the heck is this?!</i>

10:53.069 --> 10:55.738
Come here. I'll pat your head.

10:56.364 --> 10:57.198
Did he just...

10:57.281 --> 10:58.407
"Pat his head"?

10:58.491 --> 10:59.325
Right?

11:01.535 --> 11:02.536
<i>No doubt about it!</i>

11:03.037 --> 11:06.248
<i>He said it! He said he'd pat my head!</i>

11:06.957 --> 11:09.251
<i>And the way he's holding his hand...</i>

11:09.877 --> 11:13.255
<i>Irrefutable evidence, he could
only pat me on the head like that!</i>

11:13.964 --> 11:15.841
What are you doing? Come here.

11:16.842 --> 11:21.013
I... I don't understand what you mean.

11:21.597 --> 11:24.016
It's only natural I should praise you.

11:24.725 --> 11:26.060
This is ludicrous.

11:26.143 --> 11:28.062
Don't be shy. Come here.

11:28.145 --> 11:29.605
This is a fight!

11:29.689 --> 11:30.898
So what?

11:31.607 --> 11:35.027
What father wouldn't praise his son
for a great achievement?

11:38.197 --> 11:40.366
<i>This feeling...</i>

11:42.326 --> 11:46.372
<i>Fifteen centimeters below
the young man's collarbones,</i>

11:46.455 --> 11:50.584
<i>deep inside,
something akin to pain suddenly appeared.</i>

11:52.378 --> 11:55.381
<i>Even though it hurt,
he didn't want to let it go.</i>

11:57.174 --> 11:59.635
<i>A pain that is difficult to let go of.</i>

12:01.929 --> 12:03.556
I can't bear to watch.

12:03.639 --> 12:05.558
<i>How touching...</i>

12:06.934 --> 12:10.229
<i>The normalcy of being praised
by one's father</i>

12:10.312 --> 12:13.566
<i>was something he had lacked for 18 years.</i>

12:14.984 --> 12:18.612
<i>The feelings of appreciation,
accomplishment, and elation</i>

12:18.696 --> 12:20.656
<i>when praised by your father...</i>

12:21.407 --> 12:23.993
<i>the child had been
far too deprived of them.</i>

12:24.827 --> 12:26.954
<i>He had become far too unaccustomed to it.</i>

12:28.539 --> 12:29.999
You're so cruel, Dad.

12:32.001 --> 12:35.337
Telling me that you'll pat my head
at a time like this.

12:36.630 --> 12:38.674
What? You don't want it?

12:39.675 --> 12:42.344
I... I never said I...

12:45.306 --> 12:48.517
<i>His father's fist
had been gripped so tight,</i>

12:49.852 --> 12:54.482
<i>but had now relaxed so gently
and was attempting to touch him.</i>

12:55.441 --> 12:57.860
<i>"I don't care. I don't care anymore."</i>

12:58.486 --> 13:01.113
<i>"I don't care if it's a trap.
or if it's a trick."</i>

13:02.198 --> 13:05.618
<i>"It's worth it if I can be patted
by the palm of that hand."</i>

13:11.248 --> 13:13.709
No, I can't do it. I can't do this.

13:14.960 --> 13:17.797
This moment is irreplaceable.

13:18.589 --> 13:20.466
This is a fight to see who'll win.

13:21.217 --> 13:24.136
This is a competition
to see who's stronger.

13:26.722 --> 13:28.057
<i>Well said!</i>

13:28.140 --> 13:29.141
Nice...

13:29.892 --> 13:31.352
This is a good opportunity.

13:31.435 --> 13:35.648
It's a unique opportunity for you
to experience the essence of strength.

13:36.232 --> 13:38.275
Essence of strength?

13:41.403 --> 13:44.657
Missed the conscious trigger, huh?

13:45.866 --> 13:48.410
<i>I can't move a muscle.
It's like I'm in a vice!</i>

13:48.994 --> 13:53.082
So, about what "strength" is.

13:54.542 --> 13:56.794
I wanted to pat you on the head,

13:56.877 --> 13:59.338
but you rejected my desire to pat you.

13:59.421 --> 14:00.673
<i>What's going on?!</i>

14:00.756 --> 14:02.800
It's really quite easy to understand.

14:06.804 --> 14:08.180
I'm going to pat your head.

14:09.765 --> 14:11.433
Stop it!

14:11.517 --> 14:14.770
Let go of me!

14:15.896 --> 14:16.939
You're excited.

14:17.565 --> 14:20.860
<i>Strength is the power
to realize your wishes.</i>

14:21.652 --> 14:23.946
Just look at that darling face of yours.

14:25.114 --> 14:29.702
<i>The young man tacitly understood
the essence of strength.</i>

14:33.622 --> 14:34.999
How pitiful.

14:35.082 --> 14:36.458
Let go of me, dammit!

14:37.084 --> 14:40.462
How could he bully his own son like that?

14:41.088 --> 14:43.966
He's a sadist to the core.

14:44.633 --> 14:47.344
You're so greedy for praise.

14:58.230 --> 14:59.732
You're so much trouble.

15:08.365 --> 15:11.744
I'm free to kill you and free to love you.

15:12.328 --> 15:15.122
It doesn't matter
whether you reject it or not.

15:15.748 --> 15:17.958
The power to be unaffected by conditions.

15:18.584 --> 15:23.255
The power to realize your wishes
just as you desire.

15:24.340 --> 15:25.257
That is...

15:28.302 --> 15:30.512
the most basic of what strength is!

15:31.388 --> 15:34.016
"Endurance is also part of strength."

15:34.099 --> 15:37.561
"Overcoming oneself
is also part of strength."

15:38.354 --> 15:40.147
Don't lose sight!

15:40.230 --> 15:44.026
There's absolutely no need to listen
to any of that other nonsense!

15:51.241 --> 15:52.618
Awesome!

15:52.701 --> 15:54.662
He landed like a figure skater!

15:57.247 --> 15:59.458
<i>Any other explanation
is nothing more than words</i>

15:59.541 --> 16:02.169
<i>to appease those
who cannot realize their own will.</i>

16:03.253 --> 16:06.256
<i>In other words,
they're the excuses of the weak!</i>

16:09.510 --> 16:12.179
<i>You strike him with full force, Ogre?</i>

16:20.521 --> 16:24.817
<i>Strength itself is neither good nor evil.</i>

16:26.068 --> 16:28.445
<i>The strong don't endure.</i>

16:29.905 --> 16:31.949
<i>In fact, there's no need for endurance.</i>

16:33.158 --> 16:36.203
<i>Even overcoming oneself isn't necessary.</i>

16:37.788 --> 16:39.289
<i>Those excuses...</i>

16:41.208 --> 16:44.962
<i>are pollutants that cloud the purity
of strength</i>, <i>and should be eliminated!</i>

16:45.671 --> 16:48.090
<i>His father's intentions
were clearly conveyed.</i>

16:52.636 --> 16:56.807
<i>The child gets the message sent as pain,
and takes it as a lesson.</i>

17:08.527 --> 17:12.489
Your diaphragm is rising slowly,
and your breathing is shallow.

17:13.240 --> 17:15.534
I just praised you, but look at you now.

17:16.577 --> 17:18.495
<i>"You're a loser."</i>

17:19.663 --> 17:22.708
<i>That was the unignorable nuance
of what his father said.</i>

17:23.542 --> 17:27.254
<i>But, even so, he couldn't stand.
That was the state he was in.</i>

17:28.005 --> 17:29.757
I did enjoy it a little.

17:30.591 --> 17:34.094
Now, to end it with a punch
or end it with a stomp...

17:42.102 --> 17:43.812
Whoa! It's him!

17:43.896 --> 17:45.105
The living fossil!

17:45.189 --> 17:46.023
It's Pickle!

17:47.232 --> 17:49.026
What a night this is!

17:49.109 --> 17:50.027
Pi...

17:52.112 --> 17:55.282
I've thought of you many times.

18:04.083 --> 18:06.043
Just look at how jealous he is.

18:29.650 --> 18:32.069
This ain't none of your business, asshole!

18:32.152 --> 18:34.071
Fuck off!

18:35.656 --> 18:37.783
<i>These words coming from a friend...</i>

18:39.868 --> 18:42.621
<i>Pickle was from the distant past,
the Cretaceous period,</i>

18:42.704 --> 18:44.456
<i>there's no way he could know.</i>

18:45.040 --> 18:47.459
<i>Yet, there are some things
he did understand.</i>

18:48.252 --> 18:49.461
<i>He'd been scolded.</i>

18:50.879 --> 18:54.341
<i>It's the law of nature.
Butting in is prohibited.</i>

18:54.424 --> 18:56.844
<i>It's a rule
that absolutely had to be obeyed.</i>

18:57.928 --> 19:00.848
<i>The teeth that could tear
through armor from the primitive age...</i>

19:01.723 --> 19:04.852
<i>He completely trusted
that they would never break.</i>

19:06.228 --> 19:07.354
<i>But one had been busted.</i>

19:09.314 --> 19:13.235
<i>Pickle, aged 145.5 million years...</i>

19:15.571 --> 19:17.364
<i>has learned about social expectations.</i>

19:21.118 --> 19:22.870
Sorry about this unsightly incident.

19:25.455 --> 19:30.377
For this banquet that was about to end,
though I am happy that it's begun again...

19:31.587 --> 19:35.465
My son, if your friend hadn't shown up,
it would have been over!

19:35.966 --> 19:37.885
<i>I knew he'd do--</i>

19:40.345 --> 19:42.222
<i>Shall we begin, my son?</i>

19:46.810 --> 19:49.396
<i>The first trigger battle
of the modern age.</i>

19:49.980 --> 19:52.149
I knew you'd do that.

19:53.358 --> 19:55.277
<i>When his father stepped forward,</i>

19:56.153 --> 19:59.781
<i>his son, who predicted it,
intercepted him with time to spare.</i>

20:00.574 --> 20:04.411
<i>But his father had already predicted
he would intercept it.</i>

20:05.787 --> 20:08.165
Person A decides to attack.

20:08.999 --> 20:13.754
Half a second before that decision,
person B predicts it and intercepts it.

20:14.254 --> 20:16.882
Person A immediately senses
that interception,

20:16.965 --> 20:18.967
and intercepts person B's interception.

20:20.010 --> 20:22.930
That interception by person A
is predicted by person B,

20:23.013 --> 20:26.934
then person A, then person B, then...

20:30.062 --> 20:31.063
Sheesh.

20:31.772 --> 20:35.234
How long will this cycle
of interceptions continue?

20:35.317 --> 20:36.944
Just how long?

20:57.089 --> 20:58.215
Pardon me.

20:59.466 --> 21:02.803
If I could have won at the start,
I would have already done it.

21:04.179 --> 21:05.722
But since I can't do that...

21:08.934 --> 21:10.978
I can only do it this way.

21:15.148 --> 21:17.985
I've got to search. I've got to seek.

21:18.777 --> 21:23.740
Since I was born as a weak person,
my only choice is to deceive you.

21:26.326 --> 21:28.996
I want you to pardon that.

21:29.579 --> 21:30.747
Fine.

21:32.791 --> 21:36.878
Half a second before...
the scramble for the conscious trigger.

21:40.716 --> 21:41.758
I'll humor you.

21:44.303 --> 21:46.888
As your father, I accept your challenge.

21:47.472 --> 21:48.640
What?

21:49.308 --> 21:53.145
I dare you to predict,
and be the quickest to draw.

21:54.604 --> 21:57.441
<i>Like the swordsmen in olden times.</i>

21:58.608 --> 22:01.903
<i>Like the gunslingers of the past.</i>

22:04.114 --> 22:06.533
Half a second before deciding to draw.

22:07.617 --> 22:08.660
I will...

22:09.703 --> 22:12.414
I will end this foolish game!

22:12.998 --> 22:15.417
Go ahead and try.

22:16.793 --> 22:17.961
<i>I dare you!</i>
